TITLE:: Patternarium Processes
SUMMARY:: Positive interval streams and self-exciting events
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>Patternarium
RELATED:: Guides/Patternarium, Classes/PpointProcess, Classes/Prenewal, Classes/Phawkes

DESCRIPTION::
Prenewal consumes intervals; Phawkes models conditional self-excitation. Both output delta, time or fresh Events. They start with empty history at a specified origin and require no audio server for numerical use. Evaluate musical examples after loading the main Guide instruments.

SECTION:: Exponential Poisson renewal timing
For constant rate 4, draw an exponential wait by the inverse CDF. The loop excludes the RNG's possible zero endpoint.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    u.log.neg / 4
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Exponential Poisson renewal timing
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    u.log.neg / 4
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Gamma renewal timing
An Erlang distribution is gamma with integer shape. Sum three independent rate-12 exponential waits, giving mean 0.25.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    Array.fill(3, {
        var u = 1.0.rand;
        while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
        u.log.neg / 12
    }).sum
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Gamma renewal timing
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    Array.fill(3, {
        var u = 1.0.rand;
        while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
        u.log.neg / 12
    }).sum
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Weibull renewal timing
Shape 1.5 and scale 0.25 change the interval distribution.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    0.25 * u.log.neg.pow(1 / 1.5)
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Weibull renewal timing
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    0.25 * u.log.neg.pow(1 / 1.5)
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Refractory-like timing
A fixed minimum interval plus an exponential tail.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    0.1 + (u.log.neg / 8)
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Refractory-like timing
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pfunc {
    var u = 1.0.rand;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    0.1 + (u.log.neg / 8)
}, length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Approximate time-varying rate
The next wait uses the rate evaluated at the previous arrival time. This frozen-rate approximation is not an exact non-homogeneous Poisson sampler and works best when the rate changes slowly relative to waiting times. These intervals are not an iid renewal model.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pscan(Pseq([0], 16), (time: 0), { |state|
    var rate = 4 + (0.5 * (state[\time] * 0.2).sin), u = 1.0.rand, delta;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    delta = u.log.neg / rate;
    (time: state[\time] + delta, delta: delta)
}).collect { |state| state[\delta] })).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Approximate time-varying rate
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Prenewal(Pscan(Pseq([0], 16), (time: 0), { |state|
    var rate = 4 + (0.5 * (state[\time] * 0.2).sin), u = 1.0.rand, delta;
    while { u <= 0 } { u = 1.0.rand };
    delta = u.log.neg / rate;
    (time: state[\time] + delta, delta: delta)
}).collect { |state| state[\delta] })).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Self-correcting and self-exciting timing
A continuous-time self-correcting conditional-intensity model is a future specialization. Prenewal consumes intervals supplied by the user; it does not implement that intensity model itself. For nonnegative self-excitation, use link::Classes/Phawkes::.
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Phawkes(1, 0.7, 1.2, length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Waiting times drive note spacing at half scale; process dimensions select pitches. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Patternarium-Processes / Self-correcting and self-exciting timing
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Phawkes(1, 0.7, 1.2, length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\dimension] ? x[\channel] ? 0)*7 } { 0 }, dur: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\delta] ? 0.25)*0.5 } { if(x.isArray) { x[0]*0.5 } { x*0.5 } }, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::
